    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: when an owner is created, expose a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names (the acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\nTwo changes, both on the DTO/mapping layer that the create and read pipelines share (their `RespondWith*` steps all map the `Owner` entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that computes it from the stored entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause it's derived from the **stored** `Owner` (post-persist names) and marked `readOnly`, it never enters the request body and stays consistent between the create response and subsequent reads. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
